        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f6bf59f2-f80f-513b-bab6-2e063d4309af",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Okinawa, Operation Diadem, Fourth Battle of Monte Cassino, Battle of the Liri Valley\n- Places: Okinawa, Monte Cassino, Liri Valley\n- Organizations: United States Marine forces, United States Army forces, Imperial Japanese Army, U.S. Fifth Army, British Eighth Army, Allies of World War II\n- People: Dave Schreiner\n- Concepts: Pacific War, World War II, Italian Campaign of World War II, amphibious assault\n\nFacts:\n- Operation Diadem was an Allied offensive operation conducted in May 1944 by the U.S. Fifth Army and the British Eighth Army as part of the Italian Campaign of World War II.\n- Operation Diadem was also referred to as the Fourth Battle of Monte Cassino and, in Canada, as the Battle of the Liri Valley.\n- The Battle of Okinawa, codenamed Operation Iceberg, was a major Pacific War battle fought on Okinawa by United States Marine and Army forces against the Imperial Japanese Army.\n- The Battle of Okinawa included the April 1, 1945 invasion of Okinawa, which was the largest amphibious assault in the Pacific War during World War II.\n- Dave Schreiner was mortally wounded in action as a Marine during the Battle of Okinawa on June 20, 1945.\n- Dave Schreiner died on June 21, 1945, the day after he was mortally wounded during the Battle of Okinawa.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "876d8af1-e746-5030-b71f-baea8b7ff88b",
        "text": "Page: Battle of Okinawa. Sentence: The Battle of Okinawa (Japanese: 沖縄戦 , Hepburn: Okinawa-sen ) (Okinawan: 沖縄戦 , \"Uchinaa ikusa \" ), codenamed Operation Iceberg, was a major battle of the Pacific War fought on the island of Okinawa by United States Marine and Army forces against the Imperial Japanese Army and included the largest amphibious assault in the Pacific War during World War II, the April 1, 1945, invasion of Okinawa itself.\nPage: Operation Diadem. Sentence: Operation Diadem, also referred to as the Fourth Battle of Monte Cassino or, in Canada, the Battle of the Liri Valley, was an offensive operation undertaken by the Allies of World War II (U.S. Fifth Army and British Eighth Army in May 1944, as part of the Italian Campaign of World War II.\nPage: Dave Schreiner. Sentence: He was mortally wounded in action as a Marine on June 20, 1945 during the Battle of Okinawa and died the next day.",
